== Part 2: transient (probabilistic) pre-first-token failures ==
The hard-kill run above (Part 1) showed inference_retries_total staying at 0: once the
health poller (200ms interval, internal/route.DefaultPollInterval) marks the single dead
backend unhealthy, Router.Select fails on the SECOND (retry) call too, and
internal/reliability/retry.go's Do() returns the earlier lastErr WITHOUT ever reaching the
'tries>0' branch that increments inference_retries_total (retry.go:99-104) — there is no
second backend to usefully retry onto, so the implementation does not count a doomed retry.
This part demonstrates the retry mechanism itself DOES work and IS counted, using a
transient per-request failure (mock -error-rate=0.5) that never touches /healthz: health
stays 1 throughout, so every retry's Select() succeeds against the SAME backend, and a
50% chance of success on the retry attempt cleanly demonstrates both fs-01 clauses in one
population: some requests retry-and-succeed, some retry-and-exhaust-the-budget-and-fail.

